## Verdict

**0.9.0b4 is accepted for continued beta.** The corrected build passed all 7 phases on a
clean Windows 11 box with AMD Radeon 780M hardware. Both b3 open items are confirmed fixed:

- **Model-down message** is now friendly and actionable ("KimCad couldn't reach your local
  AI. Make sure Ollama is running, then try again.") — not the generic b3 HTTP 500.
  Console: 0 errors during model-down. "Try again" flow worked end-to-end.
  Evidence: `evidence/004/24-model-down.png`, `evidence/004/24-model-down.txt`.

- **Coaster height capped at 15 mm.** `h` slider max is 15 mm (was 40 mm in b3), current
  value 10 mm for a 90 mm coaster. Evidence: `evidence/004/26-coaster.png`.

All 3 curated landing chips built on qwen2.5:7b (Phase 5a, 3/3 PASS, 0 console errors).
Custom design + slider re-render + slice + export (.stl + .3mf) functional (Phase 5b).
Photo/sketch on-ramp live on qwen2.5vl:3b (Phase 5e). Keyboard viewport navigation PASS
(Phase 5f). All 6 connector types graceful (Phase 6). Clean uninstall with user data
correctly retained (Phase 7). WebGL rendered on real 780M via ANGLE/D3D11.
